<title>USA: TABLE - Autotote Corp sells 144a notes.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Autotote Corp sells 144a notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144a debt issue from Autotote Corp was priced Monday via sole manager Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jenrette Securities, according to a market source.</p>
<p>Autotote makes, operates parimutual wafering equipment for horse, and greyhound tracks.</p>
<p>BORROWER AUTOTOTE CORP</p>
<p>AMT $110 MLN	 COUPON 10.875 PCT MATURITY 8/1/2004</p>
<p>TYPE SNR NOTES     ISS PRICE 100.00  FIRST PAY DATE 2/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S B2    YIELD 10.875 PCT  PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P B-PLUS			    CALLABLE  NON-CALL FOUR</p>
<p>NOTES: The notes have a three-year equity call for 35 percent of the issue at 110.875.</p>
<p>((U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
</text>
